script = ExtResource("1_rd28n")
dialogue_id = "debate_monk_rulers"
record_title = "Debate Speech: The Monk Rulers"
text = "PAGE: historian(PORTAL_NETWORK), AUDIENCE
historian: Let us look, today, at the fate of the shard that held our very first shrine in the New World.
historian: Centuries ago, the priests there decided to bar laypeople from entering a shrine after some fences were damaged.
historian: It seems a harmless precaution, but over the centuries this elevation of the divine over the mundane has had dire consequences.
historian: When my friend the Explorer visited the shard, he was arrested for nothing more than writing in his journal.
historian: You see, literacy on this shard is a privilege reserved for the holy order.
historian: When we allow our priests to control our laws, we create a dangerous hierarchy.
historian: A city council answers to the citizens.
historian: A holy magistrate answers to none but the spirits.
historian: And who is to say whether spirits are just?
historian: Who, indeed, but the priests themselves?
historian: I believe we are capable of developing our own morals, learning from our successes and failures, and adapting to the needs of the age.
historian: The Scribe believes that uniting us under a single religious mandate will bring universal harmony.
historian: But this shard's story is a lesson to us all about what happens when faith becomes the law."
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://jtkfcsyiryo4"
